Module(
  body=[
    Expr(
      value=Constant(value='\nGolden State Evaluator (v10_10 · Phase 3 — Batch D)\n===================================================\n\nThis module provides a deterministic evaluation harness for the v10_10\nagentic workflow.\n\nIt is deliberately *pure*:\n\n    • No LLM calls.\n    • No orchestration, execution, or planning.\n    • Only consumes already‑materialised runtime artefacts\n      (typically the final L4 state patch exported as JSON).\n\nThe main responsibilities are:\n\n    1. Define *golden* evaluation scenarios that exercise the\n       Phase‑3 control knobs and capabilities (G1–G37), in\n       particular:\n\n           • HYDE on vs HYDE off\n           • RRF strategy variants\n           • QA council size (1 vs N)\n           • Correction‑loop depth (0 → N)\n           • Telemetry‑aware routing modes\n           • Deterministic "golden mode" configuration\n\n    2. Provide deterministic, machine‑verifiable scoring of a\n       *single* workflow patch against a GoldenExpectation.\n\n    3. Expose a small CLI suitable for CI/CD:\n\n           python -m golden_eval              --patch run_output.json              --expectation golden_expectations.json              --scenario-id hyde_on_weighted              --out eval_report.json\n\nThe actual execution of the workflow (calling main_v10_10 or\nrun_batch_v10_10) is *not* handled here; that is the job of\nsimulation.py and separate test harnesses.  This module only\ndefines scenarios and evaluates data.\n')),
    ImportFrom(
      module='__future__',
      names=[
        alias(name='annotations')],
      level=0),
    ImportFrom(
      module='dataclasses',
      names=[
        alias(name='dataclass'),
        alias(name='field'),
        alias(name='asdict'),
        alias(name='is_dataclass')],
      level=0),
    ImportFrom(
      module='enum',
      names=[
        alias(name='Enum')],
      level=0),
    ImportFrom(
      module='pathlib',
      names=[
        alias(name='Path')],
      level=0),
    ImportFrom(
      module='typing',
      names=[
        alias(name='Any'),
        alias(name='Dict'),
        alias(name='Iterable'),
        alias(name='List'),
        alias(name='Mapping'),
        alias(name='Optional'),
        alias(name='Sequence')],
      level=0),
    Import(
